      "orig": "This article  investigates  the  dynamics  of  social  networks  in shaping public debate, with an emphasis on Twitter (currently called X) and the influence of algorithms on content regulation. Using an interdisciplinary approach that integrates concepts from Digital Sociology and Computer Science, the study analyzes how curation and moderation mechanisms -operated  by private companies -affect  the  construction  of  discourses  and  the  dissemination  of information. The research brings together empirical data, academic analyses and journalistic reports to demonstrate that changes in moderation policies,",
